{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2958","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2958","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2958\",\"parent_revision\":\"57b6cd9bd29b3196e27a12f2228c35132ffa3ef7\",\"root_revision\":\"aa924e94f3ea641216417545f3c36f8c88c1e86409258f88c9dd9ffe17fdd9e1\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-18\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md`'s Output Validation Gate requires the RT-ICA section to satisfy: \\\"Contains `Decision: APPROVED` or `Decision: BLOCKED` and `Date: YYYY-MM-DD`.\\\" The `dh:rtica-assessor` agent, dispatched during `swarm.md`'s Wave 2 to produce this same section, returns and reports its own result as \\\"Verdict: READY\\\" or presumably \\\"Verdict: BLOCKED\\\" \u2014 not \\\"Decision: APPROVED\\\"/\\\"Decision: BLOCKED\\\". Confirmed live on #2953: the rtica-assessor teammate's final response stated \\\"**Verdict: READY for planning**\\\" and its written RT-ICA section content used that same \\\"READY\\\" vocabulary, not the literal string `finalize.md` checks for.\\n\\nAs documented, the output-validation gate's literal content check can never pass against the actual output format the designated agent produces for that section, without an undocumented manual reconciliation step by the orchestrator (translating \\\"READY\\\" to \\\"APPROVED\\\" by inference). This either means every real grooming pass silently fails the documented validation gate's stated content requirement, or orchestrators have been informally translating between the two vocabularies without that being part of the documented workflow \u2014 either way, the finalize.md spec and the rtica-assessor agent's actual output contract are out of sync with each other.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **rt-ica vocabulary mismatch: rtica-assessor returns \\\"verdict: ready/blocked\\\" but finalize.md's output-validation gate literally requires \\\"decision: approved/blocked\\\"** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 discovered during retrospective sweep of groom-workflow docs while grooming #2953, 2026-08-18\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-18\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"7abe1673a9400f5cf9c0dd28e3bf39248785d3a10e3f8516449c031077720c94\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPUXLMg\"}"}